      "summary": "Delivered the host bringup for the 8-GPU flagship under TP8.ZeRO-3, all three gate_commands green (rc=0), committed at 0b66169.\n\n(1) THE TP WEIGHT-SHARD — grokking_optimizers/distributed.py::partition_tensor_parallel(named_sizes, tp, tp_rank, model=\"decoder\") + TPShardPlan/TPTensorShard. Megatron column/row split: in_proj (3d x d) and ff.0 (4d x d) split on the output-feature dim (column-parallel), out_proj (d x d) and ff.2 (d x 4d) split on the input-feature dim (row-parallel), embeddings/norms/biases/unembed replicated. Proven: per-rank Nmax = kDecMaxTensorNumel/TP = 10,240,000/8 = 1,280,000 exactly (the load-bearing memory claim that makes the SG2 staged-opt scratch fit); tp=1 is the byte-identical fold (everything replicated, total preserved); loud ValueError when tp does not divide a split dim. Exported in __all__.\n\n(2) THE HOST NVSHMEM TP-TEAM BOOTSTRAP — NEW grokking_optimizers/host_bringup.py (re-exported from distributed.py as TPBootstrap/bootstrap_tp_team). Mirrors the launcher EDIT E contract bit-for-bit: tp_heap_stride_floats(ctas_per_pe) = ctas_per_pe*2*kTileM(128)*kD(1600) sizes the collective nvshmem_malloc symmetric heap (3,276,800 floats at ctas_per_pe=8, == dec_tc_ensure_tp_sym_heap); TPBootstrap.pe_range() computes the nvshmem_team_split_strided (PE_start, PE_stride, PE_size) from the TP-fastest Megatron linearization (single-node pure-TP -> (0,1,8) == NVSHMEM_TEAM_WORLD, the launcher fast-path; DP2xTP4 -> the strided sub-range); the TP team id is encoded into CommCtx.tp_comm_handle as the void*-cast int32 (round-trip verified, matches tp::make_transport_from_comm reverse-cast). bootstrap_tp_team(allow_dry=True) validates on CPU; the live path discovers libnvshmem_host.so.3 (present) and raises a PRECISE TPBootstrapBlocked scoping the genuine blocker — no nvshmem Python binding + no launcher nvshmem_init pybind on this box, so the live C init/team-split/malloc stays the launcher TU's job (route (a) pybind or (b) MPI/PMIX plugin spelled out).\n\n(3) THE TORCHRUN HARNESS — NEW tuning/flagship_distributed.py + NEW grokking_optimizers/parallel/flagship_budget.py. The harness builds the flagship TC megakernel per rank (flagship.md layout swap + ParConfig TP degrees + optional -DSG_HAS_NVSHMEM=1 RDC link), seeds identically, runs the in-kernel-TP fused step, and verifies cross-rank loss agreement (all_gather fp64, assert <1e-9) + A/A/A param-checksum. The --dry-run --model decoder --gpus 8 validates the full 4D mesh + TP weight-shard + symmetric-heap stride + tp_comm_handle + per-rank HBM budget for all 8 ranks on CPU (no GPU, no NVSHMEM init) — the cheap pre-flight before the expensive flagship compile.\n\nNo csrc/kernel edits, so the MANDATORY decoder TC SingleGPU path is byte-identical by construction; gfx942/tpu untouched. Regression: pytest -k \"parallel or distributed or zero3\" = 30 passed, 2 skipped, 0 failed.\n\nKEY FILES (absolute): /workspace/SuperGrok1.5/.claude/worktrees/wf_fa93283c-3c7-2/grokking_optimizers/distributed.py (partition_tensor_parallel + TP shard types + TPBootstrap re-export); /workspace/SuperGrok1.5/.claude/worktrees/wf_fa93283c-3c7-2/grokking_optimizers/host_bringup.py (NVSHMEM TP-team bootstrap); /workspace/SuperGrok1.5/.claude/worktrees/wf_fa93283c-3c7-2/grokking_optimizers/parallel/flagship_budget.py; /workspace/SuperGrok1.5/.claude/worktrees/wf_fa93283c-3c7-2/tuning/flagship_distributed.py.\n\nLIVE-RUN BLOCKER (scoped): the 8-GPU device-initiated NVSHMEM all-reduce needs the launcher TU to expose an nvshmem_init/team_split pybind (it already links nvshmem behind -DSG_HAS_NVSHMEM=1 and calls nvshmem_team_my_pe/NVSHMEM_TEAM_WORLD), driven by a torch.distributed broadcast of nvshmemx_get_uniqueid(); OR launch under the MPI/PMIX bootstrap plugin (nvshmem_bootstrap_mpi.so.3 present) with NVSHMEM_BOOTSTRAP=MPI. The host plan/shard/heap math is fully validated and ready; this is purely the cross-process NVSHMEM init seam (dist_step.md §6.D)."
